a. $A=\{2,4,6\}$ and $B=\{1,2,3\}$. Place $2$ in the overlap, $4,6$ in $A$ only, $1,3$ in $B$ only and $5$ outside both.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=10mm,y=10mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},draw=black]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (7,4);
\draw (2.5,2) circle (1.5);
\draw (4.5,2) circle (1.5);
\node at (1.7,3.65) {$A$};
\node at (5.3,3.65) {$B$};
\node at (1.9,2) {$4,6$};
\node at (3.5,2) {$2$};
\node at (5.1,2) {$1,3$};
\node at (6.5,0.5) {$5$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

b. Non-mutually exclusive: the overlap contains $2$, which satisfies both conditions.

c. Mutually exclusive: $\{1,2,3\}$ and $\{5,6\}$ share no outcome. Rolling $4$ belongs to neither event.

There are $26$ black cards and $4$ jacks. The jack of spades and jack of clubs belong to both events.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=10mm,y=10mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},draw=black]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (7,4);
\draw (2.5,2) circle (1.5);
\draw (4.5,2) circle (1.5);
\node at (1.7,3.65) {Black};
\node at (5.3,3.65) {Jack};
\node at (1.9,2) {$24$};
\node at (3.5,2) {$2$};
\node at (5.1,2) {$2$};
\node at (6.5,0.5) {$24$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

a. Inclusive or includes all black cards and the two red jacks, counting each black jack once.

$\begin{aligned}P(\text{black or jack, or both})&=\frac{24+2+2}{52}\\&=\frac{28}{52}\\&=\frac{7}{13}\end{aligned}$

b. Exclusive or excludes both black jacks. Include the $24$ black cards that are not jacks and the $2$ red jacks.

$\begin{aligned}P(\text{black or jack, but not both})&=\frac{24+2}{52}\\&=\frac{26}{52}\\&=\frac{1}{2}\end{aligned}$
